Make the PWA surface honor RAILS_RELATIVE_URL_ROOT.

Sure supports sub-path hosting: with RAILS_RELATIVE_URL_ROOT set (sure-nix
mounts the app under it via Rack::URLMap in config.ru), Rails path helpers and
asset URLs carry the prefix. The PWA surface is the one part that does not —
it hardcodes the domain root — so under a sub-path every piece of it breaks:

  * app/views/pwa/manifest.json.erb — `start_url` and `scope` are "/", and the
    icon `src`s are "/logo-pwa.png" etc. The icons 404, and the installed app
    is scoped to (and launches at) the domain root, which is not Sure.
  * app/views/layouts/shared/_head.html.erb — the apple-touch-icon and icon
    links are root-absolute, so iOS "Add to Home Screen" gets no icon.
  * app/javascript/application.js — registers "/service-worker", which 404s,
    so the worker never installs and offline support is silently dead.
  * app/views/pwa/service-worker.js — caches "/offline.html" and
    "/logo-offline.svg"; those 404 too, so cache.addAll() rejects and fails the
    install event even if registration is fixed.

Files under public/ are served by the web server rather than the asset
pipeline, so they get no prefix automatically; splice on `root_path`, which is
"/" at the domain root and "<prefix>/" under one. The service worker resolves
its assets against `self.location` instead, since it is plain JS with no ERB.
application.js is a static importmap asset for the same reason, so it reads the
prefix from a new `app-base-path` meta tag rendered in the shared head.

Every change is an identity transform when RAILS_RELATIVE_URL_ROOT is unset, so
root-hosted deployments are unaffected. Base patch (on by default).

diff --git a/app/javascript/application.js b/app/javascript/application.js
index 353017f..d00f1ab 100644
--- a/app/javascript/application.js
+++ b/app/javascript/application.js
@@ -53,7 +53,12 @@ Turbo.StreamActions.redirect = function () {
 // Register service worker for PWA offline support
 if ('serviceWorker' in navigator) {
   window.addEventListener('load', () => {
-    navigator.serviceWorker.register('/service-worker')
+    // Mount prefix ("/" at the domain root, e.g. "/sure/" under
+    // RAILS_RELATIVE_URL_ROOT) — see the app-base-path meta tag in
+    // layouts/shared/_head. A root-absolute '/service-worker' 404s when the app
+    // is hosted under a sub-path, so the registration silently never happens.
+    const appBasePath = document.querySelector('meta[name="app-base-path"]')?.content || '/';
+    navigator.serviceWorker.register(`${appBasePath}service-worker`)
       .then(registration => {
         console.log('Service Worker registered with scope:', registration.scope);
       })
diff --git a/app/views/layouts/shared/_head.html.erb b/app/views/layouts/shared/_head.html.erb
index 91ea791..08b0381 100644
--- a/app/views/layouts/shared/_head.html.erb
